00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:04.390 align:start position:0%
 
hey folks welcome back to scp explained  sorry if i seem a little out of it today  truth be told i've been having real  trouble sleeping lately perhaps it's  because i spend so much time pouring  through the files of the scp foundation  archive also i've been catching up on  the west wing there's plenty of  creatures entities objects and tales  that are very effective at making you  lose sleep but none quite as effective  as  scp-966 grab yourself a pot of coffee  and prop your eyelids open with some  matchsticks or tape because you need to  stay alert if you want to survive this  one though when you get on the wrong  side of scp-966  i'm sorry to tell you that your chances  of survival are extremely low and after  experiencing its primary anomalous  effects the question of how long you'll  even want to survive will become  disturbingly prescient like many of our  explorations into the living nightmares  that the scp foundation deals with on a  daily basis the best way to experience  exactly what  scp-966 can do is to take a look at a  case study regarding one of its many  unfortunate victims in this case that  victim is a man named terry hallberg  from new mexico in another life perhaps  terry would have been an ideal candidate  for a junior researcher position at the  scp foundation he was a  scientific-minded truth-seeker whose  interests lied in the more esoteric  fields of study namely ghosts and aliens  proving the existence of life in the  stars and the supernatural in general  was something he considered to be his  life's work this is why he moved to new  mexico home of roswell and widely  considered to be the ufo capital of the  united states in the first place there  he'd perform experiments on a wide range  of bizarre phenomenon from exploring  haunted houses to obsessively watching  the sky for any anomalous activity he'd  become a big wig in his niche online  paranormal investigation community and  his posts on the somewhat infamous  periwatch forum always garnered plenty  of attention but terry wanted more he  wasn't in it for the fame or the money  or the legions of insatiable paranormal  investigator groupies he was a true  believer he wanted a close first-hand  experience with the supernatural and  that was exactly what he was about to  get in addition to a very harsh lesson  about being careful what you wish for it  began when he got called out to  albuquerque for a strange case of cattle  mutilation for those who don't frequent  the parawatch forums quite as often as  terry cattle mutilation is the most  common nickname for the phenomenon of  large livestock usually cows being found  dead with unusual mutilation patterns on  their corpses while the particulars of  what exactly this means varies from  believer to believer with theories  ranging from aliens to black helicopters  it is widely accepted across all  branches of paranormal enthusiasts that  when cattle are being mutilated  something very strange is afoot terry  arrived at the ranch and with the  application of a little cache to grease  the appropriate palms he was able to  conduct a recorded interview with the  rancher he was a weathered man in his  early 60s with a somewhat frantic  demeanor and profoundly tired eyes when  terry asked him if he'd experienced any  unusual phenomenon in the days leading  up to the cattle mutilation incident he  was surprisingly forthcoming about the  hellish conditions he'd been  experiencing lately the strange  experiences had been going on for  several days now it all started when the  rancher noticed that a number of his  cows weren't sleeping this isn't the  easiest thing to spot in a cow because  cattle engage in what is known as  polyphasic sleep where instead of  sleeping for one prolonged period like  humans typically do they sleep in small  intervals throughout a 24 hour period  cows can even sleep standing up for  periods of light rest but during rem  sleep which all mammals need for healthy  functioning they lay down just like us  the problem was in the last several days  many of the ranchers cows hadn't slept  at all it was after this that the  ranchers seemingly begin to have bizarre  paranormal experiences himself it began  with a general sense of unease and dread  which was soon followed by a sense of  severe insomnia that had left him  completely unable to sleep for the past  two days during this period things had  gotten worse he'd experienced strange  noises around his home footsteps what  sounded like hushed voices and  occasionally even what could only be  identified as a low croaking growl but  it wasn't just noises there was also  physical evidence of some kind of  intrusion  items had been knocked over or moved at  one point a glass of water which had  been centralized on a stable surface had  somehow fallen off the edge and  shattered the old rancher with a  trembling voice even stated that he'd  seen things moving in the corners of his  eyes figures  shapes little green men and then the  cattle mutilation spree began it may  have sounded morbid but terry had to use  everything in his power to stop himself  from smiling ear to ear well this was a  terrifying experience for the rancher  for terry this was an absolutely  textbook case of paranormal experience  and here he was the very first person to  document it all it could be the next  skinwalker ranch or rental shum forest  incident and his name would forever be  attached to it he asked the rancher if  he could see the cow's body and the  rancher obliged whatever had caused this  alien ghost or otherwise had really done  a number on this cow good portions of  its abdomen had been torn away with  evidence of what appeared to be biting  and clawing this poor beast had been  eaten alive while exploring the wounds  with a magnifying glass a scalpel and a  large pair of tweezers terry discovered  something incredible something frankly  unprecedented for a cattle mutilation  case a piece of evidence left behind  directly by whatever had perpetrated  this act of gruesome violence a long  thin and exceedingly sharp claw around  12 centimeters in length and broken at  one end new mexico's large predators  included mountain lions black bears  bobcats and coyotes and this claw was  nothing like any of those in fact it was  nothing like terry had ever seen before  was this his big moment had he  discovered evidence of an entirely new  supernatural creature or specimen of  extraterrestrial life he was practically  vibrating with excitement about this new  discovery after thanking and paying the  rancher again terry took some photos  gathered some more samples and laughed  he had everything he needed to conduct a  groundbreaking investigation into the  supernatural just wait until the folks  on parawatch heard about this in all his  excitement as he drove back home from  the ranch he never once stopped to  consider what he might be bringing back  with him but really in the end it didn't  even matter from the moment he stepped  onto that ranch terry hallberg was  already doomed he just didn't know it  yet he arrived home and began to record  all of his information onto one master  document he also began obsessively  assembling outside research hoping to  find similar cases that he could add to  this emerging pattern it was a mix of  phenomenon from both hauntings and alien  encounters could this possibly be some  form of alien ghost the dream find of  every paranormal investigator terry had  to steal his racing heart as the  possibilities bombarded his mind he  could have been working with the  paranormal find of the century here in  fact he was so excited by all of this he  didn't even realize that he worked  through the entire night he didn't sleep  a wink after all how could you when such  important research needed to be done the  burst of nocturnal energy felt like a  godsend the next night not so much in  the meantime terry had compiled his  information together enough to present  it to his esteemed paranormal colleagues  on the periwatch forums they were  startled and amazed by what they were  seeing and hearing especially the taped  interview with the rancher and the  mysterious claw one of terry's closest  associates who went by the username john  station pulled up a similar bizarre case  of a los angeles hiker who died in the  hills in the days before his death his  family and friends reported him  complaining about insomnia and  experiencing an increasing state of  paranoia and distress he started taking  long walks across remote trails in hopes  of tiring himself out enough to finally  get some sleep but that time never came  when his corpse was found it was mauled  and half eaten everyone assumed that a  mountain lion had killed him and other  scavengers had fed on him before his  body was found but now terry wasn't so  sure the more they looked into it the  more they found strange and unpleasant  deaths connected to people suffering  from what seemed like severe insomnia  despite its debilitating effects the  only type of insomnia that directly  causes death is the exceedingly rare  genetic condition fatal familial  insomnia which couldn't account for the  sheer number of deaths the parawatch  team were finding in their minds there  was only one reasonable conclusion the  deaths weren't the result of the  insomnia itself but whatever was causing  it it was only then that terry noticed  his own inability to sleep and his  previous excitement was gradually  replaced with panic at first he try to  keep it all in proportion knowing that  it's easy to invent things to fear when  you're in uncharted territory but as the  days passed and the sleep never came his  worry became unassailable terry knew  that he hadn't just discovered a new  paranormal phenomenon he was becoming  one of its victims he became  increasingly paranoid over the next few  days taking constant evp readings from  around his apartment in hopes of  detecting whatever was around him there  were strange noises frightening noises  he just knew it but little did poor  terry know there was a very good reason  he couldn't detect his tormentors while  he had been in his apartment for days  now he had no hope of ever seeing them  the humanized spectrum of visible light  is around 380 to 750 nanometers but the  monsters who deprived him of his ability  to sleep existed somewhere around 900  they were entirely undetectable to the  human eye and they were waiting for  their latest meal as the insomnia grew  worse terry received some frightening  news that rancher who he'd spoken to a  few days before was found dead on his  property with severe injuries comparable  to that of a wild animal attack just  like his cattle and just like all the  other strange cases the parawatch forum  had found first the insomnia then the  frightening paranormal experiences and  then  terry found something warm and wet  trickling down the back of his neck he  probably would have realized it was his  own blood if a 20 centimeter claw just  like the one he had pulled out of the  dead cow hadn't just pierced his brain  stem terry hallberg had finally gotten  what he wanted a first-hand experience  with the supernatural and all he had to  do  was die but in his defense being saved  from  scp-966 a whole species of monsters  known as the sleep killers is almost  worse than being killed by them when  they release their deadly energy pulse  their primary anomalous effect which  induces sleeplessness on anyone or  anything in their immediate 20 meter  radius the effects are permanent they  essentially induce fatal insomnia and  your only options are to die by their  claws or live long enough to see your  own body and mind give out from the  horrible effects of true sleep  deprivation they travel in pairs and  because of their invisibility you never  know when they're lurking around you  waiting to rob you of your sleep and  then your life the foundation currently  has four specimens in containment but  believe us there are a lot more out  there and they're hungry sleep tight if  you can now go check out killer living  graffiti scp-1155 predatory street art  and waldo finds you  scp-4885 find him for more terrifying  monsters that'll hunt you to your last  breath

